Instructions for cobcd.py, version 0.5 and newer.

The key to making cobcd.py work is to load it in into your debugging session.

This may be done via your personal ~/.gdbinit file.
However: ./python/make install now takes care of it.

Remove any ~/.gdbinit instructions that look like

    source ~/projects/cobol/batch-demo/gdb/python/cobcd.py
    directory ~/projects/cobol/batch-demo/gdb/python
    add-auto-load-safe-path ~/projects/cobol/batch-demo/gdb/python

You can leave this next one; if you take it out, the install will put it back in

    set auto-load python-scripts on

As an alternative cobcd may include it in the binaries - or you just source it
manually / use a gdb wrapper scr
ipt for that.
